{
  "category_id": 11,
  "category_name": "Quranic Duas",
  "duas": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "category_id": 11,
      "title": "Surah al-Fatihah: The Greatest Duʿa",
      "title_ar": null,
      "arabic": "بِسْمِ اللّٰهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ ، اَلْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ رَبِّ الْعَالَمِيْنَ ، الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ ، مٰلِكِ يَوْمِ الدِّيْنِ ، إِيَّاكَ نَعْبُدُ وَإِيَّاكَ نَسْتَعِيْنُ ، اِهْدِنَا الصِّرَاطَ الْمُسْتَقِيْمَ ، صِرَاطَ الَّذِيْنَ أَنْعَمْتَ عَلَيْهِمْ غَيْرِ الْمَغْضُوْبِ عَلَيْهِمْ وَلَا الضَّآلِّيْنَ.",
      "transliteration": "Bismi-llāhi-r-Raḥmāni-r-Raḥīm. Alḥamdu-lillāhi Rabbi-l-ʿālamīn, ar-Raḥmāni-r-Raḥīm, Māliki yawmi-d-dīn, iyyāka naʿbudu wa iyyāka nastaʿīn, ihdina-ṣ-Ṣirāṭa-l-Mustaqīm, ṣirāṭa-lladhīna anʿamta ʿalayhim ghayri-l-maghḍūbi ʿālayhim wa la-ḍ-ḍāllīn. We often read Sūrah al-Fātiḥah, but we sometimes forget that it is one of the most powerful and comprehensive du’ās. This du‘ā’ is so amazing because: 1\\. We are taught the ‘adab’ (etiquette) of making du’ā’: Praise Him with His Most Beautiful Names and Attributes, express our servitude to Him and THEN ask Him.",
      "translation": "In the name of Allah, the All-Merciful, the Very Merciful. All praises and thanks are for Allah, the Lord of all the worlds, The All-Merciful, The Very Merciful, Master of the Day of Judgement. You Alone we worship, You Alone we ask for help. Guide us on the Straight Path, the path of those whom You have favoured, not of those who incur (Your) anger nor of those who have gone astray. (1:1-7)",
      "virtue": "## Why This Dua is Essential\n\n**We are asking Allah for guidance** - It can only come from Him. When we are guided by Allah, He helps us to obey Him and to stop sinning. When this happens, we are saved from all evil in this world and the hereafter.\n\n**Why keep repeating this dua?** We might think to ourselves: 'We are already guided. Why do we need to keep repeating this duʿā?' Consider:\n- Sometimes we may know the truth but we are not able to act upon it\n- Or we may act upon it, but we may lack sincerity in our actions\n- Or maybe it doesn't conform to the Sunnah of the Messenger ﷺ\n- And more importantly, today we might be upon 'guidance', but what about tomorrow?\n\n**Comprehensive protection** - 'Guide us on the straight path' is a duʿā for all of the above AND firmness on the path. We are asking Allah to keep us firm on this path (al-ṣirāt al-mustaqīm) so that we can pass over the bridge (Ṣirāṭ) in the hereafter as smoothly and as quickly as possible.",
      "reference": "",
      "repetitions": null,
      "order": 1,
      "tags": [
        "Quranic Duas",
        "Quran"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "category_id": 11,
      "title": "Duʿa of the Grief-stricken Prophet Yunus ﷺ",
      "title_ar": null,
      "arabic": "لَآ إِلٰهَ إِلَّآ أَنْتَ سُبْحَانَكَ إِنِّيْ كُنْتُ مِنَ الظَّالِمِيْنَ.",
      "transliteration": "Lā ilāha illā Anta subḥānaka innī kuntu mina-ẓ-ẓālimīn.",
      "translation": "There is no god worthy of worship except You. You are free from imperfection. Indeed, I have been of the wrongdoers. (21:87)",
      "virtue": "## Ask Allah Through His Oneness\n\nCalling upon Allah through His Oneness is one of the most powerful ways to make duʿā. The grief-stricken Prophet Yunus (ʿalayhis-salām) cried out to his Lord: **لا اله الا انت سبحانك اني كنت من الظالمين**\n\nThe Prophet ﷺ said that **no one supplicates with this duʿa except that his supplication is accepted**. And nobody supplicates with it except that **Allah removes his difficulties**. (Tirmidhi)\n\n## The Three Steps of Tawassul\n\nIn this duʿa, Yunus ﷺ asked Allah through the following steps (known as tawassul in Arabic):\n\n1. **Invoking the Oneness of Allah** and affirming that no one deserves to be worshipped except Him\n2. **Declaring Allah's absolute perfection** and negating any faults from Him\n3. **Acknowledging one's own wrongdoing**",
      "reference": "",
      "repetitions": null,
      "order": 2,
      "tags": [
        "Quranic Duas",
        "Prophet"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "category_id": 11,
      "title": "Duʿa of Prophet Musa ﷺ for Forgiveness",
      "title_ar": null,
      "arabic": "رَبِّ إِنِّيْ ظَلَمْتُ نَفْسِيْ فَاغْفِرْ لِيْ.",
      "transliteration": "Rabbi innī ẓalamtu nafsī fa-ghfirlī. This is the du‘ā’ Musā (‘alayhis-salām) made after he unintentionally killed a Coptic man. He realised that it was only through turning to Allah (subḥānahū wa ta‘ālā) that he could make things right. He cried out ‘My Rabb’. We too should cry out to our ‘Rabb’ when we have wronged.",
      "translation": "My Lord, I have certainly wronged myself, so forgive me. (28:16)",
      "virtue": "We should then acknowledge our sins, as acknowledging one’s sins and shortcomings is a sunnah of the Prophets and Messengers (‘alayhimus-Salām). And thereafter, we should ask Allah to forgive us.",
      "reference": "",
      "repetitions": null,
      "order": 3,
      "tags": [
        "Quranic Duas",
        "Forgiveness",
        "Prophet"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "category_id": 11,
      "title": "Duʿa of Prophet Adam ﷺ and Hawwa for Forgiveness",
      "title_ar": null,
      "arabic": "رَبَّنَا ظَلَمْنَآ أَنْفُسَنَا وَإِنْ لَّمْ تَغْفِرْ لَنَا وَتَرْحَمْنَا لَنَكُوْنَنَّ مِنَ الْخٰسِرِيْنَ.",
      "transliteration": "Rabbanā ẓalamnā anfusanā wa il-lam taghfir lanā wa tarḥamnā la-nakūnanna minal-khāsīrīn. This is the du‘ā’ of our father Ādam (‘alayhis-salām) and mother Ḥawwā’ (‘alayhas-salām) after they had been lured by Shayṭān to eat from the tree. What we can learn from this du‘ā’:",
      "translation": "Our Lord, we have wronged ourselves. If You do not forgive us and have mercy upon us, we will surely be amongst the losers. (7:23)",
      "virtue": "## Lessons From This Dua\n\n**1. Acknowledge sins first** - We should acknowledge our sins and shortcomings before asking for forgiveness\n\n**2. Combine fear and hope** - This duʿā contains fear (we will surely be amongst the losers) and hope (mercy and forgive). We too, should combine fear and hope in our duʿās\n\n**3. Show remorse** - We should show our remorse and turn to Allah in humility, like our parents did\n\n**4. Learn from the contrast** - We see the difference in attitude between Ādam (ʿalayhis-salām) and Shayṭān:\n- **Ādam (ʿalayhis-salām)**: Acknowledged his mistake, felt remorse over it, blamed himself for it, hastened to repent and didn't lose hope from the mercy of Allah\n- **Shayṭān**: Didn't acknowledge his sin, didn't feel remorse, attributed blame to his Lord, didn't repent and lost hope in the mercy of Allah",
      "reference": "",
      "repetitions": null,
      "order": 4,
      "tags": [
        "Quranic Duas",
        "Forgiveness",
        "Prophet"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "category_id": 11,
      "title": "Duʿa of Prophet Musa ﷺ for Forgiveness",
      "title_ar": null,
      "arabic": "أَنْتَ وَلِيُّنَا فَاغْفِرْ لَنَا وَارْحَمْنَا ۖ وَأَنْتَ خَيْرُ الْغَافِرِيْنَ.",
      "transliteration": "Anta Walliyyunā fa-ghfir lanā war-ḥamnā wa Anta khayrul-ghāfirīn. In this du‘ā’ Mūsā (‘alayhis-salām) asked Allah (subḥānahū wa ta‘ālā) for forgiveness and mercy. He asked through Allah’s name ‘al-Waliyy’. Al-Waliyy is the Protective Friend, the Helper, the Patron, the One who truly loves us. Waliyy is derived from ‘wilāyah’ which denotes closeness, loyalty and authority. Whilst Allah’s general wilāyah extends to all of creation, His special wilāyah is reserved for the believers who are extra-devoted to Him.",
      "translation": "You are our Protector, so forgive us and have mercy upon us. You are the best of those who forgive. (7:155)",
      "virtue": "## Hadith\nThe Messenger of Allah ﷺ said:\n\n**\"“Then, my servant continues to draw near to me with voluntary worship until I love Him, and when I love him, I become his hearing that he hears with, his sight that he sees with, his hand by which he grasps, and his feet by which he walks.” (Bukhārī)\"**",
      "reference": "",
      "repetitions": null,
      "order": 5,
      "tags": [
        "Quranic Duas",
        "Forgiveness",
        "Prophet"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "category_id": 11,
      "title": "Duʿa of the Pious for Forgiveness & Protection From the Hell-fire",
      "title_ar": null,
      "arabic": "رَبَّنَآ إِنَّنَآ اٰمَنَّا فَاغْفِرْ لَنَا ذُنُوْبَنَا وَقِنَا عَذَابَ النَّارِ.",
      "transliteration": "Rabbanā in-nanā āmannā fa-ghfir lanā dhunūbanā wa qinā ʿadhāba-n-nār. This is the du‘ā’ of the people of piety and faith. In this du‘ā’, we learn a permissible and commendable form of tawassul (asking Allah through something). In this case, we are asking through one of the greatest actions of a human being: imān. It is as though we are saying, ‘O Allah, we have believed. Therefore, through and because of our belief, forgive us and protect us from Hell-fire.’",
      "translation": "Our Lord, indeed we have believed, so forgive us our sins and protect us from the punishment of the Fire. (3:16)",
      "virtue": "",
      "reference": "",
      "repetitions": null,
      "order": 6,
      "tags": [
        "Quranic Duas",
        "Protection",
        "Forgiveness"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "category_id": 11,
      "title": "Duʿa of the Slaves of Allah for Forgiveness & Mercy",
      "title_ar": null,
      "arabic": "رَبَّنَآ اٰمَنَّا فَاغْفِرْ لَنَا وَارْحَمْنَا وَأَنْتَ خَيْرُ الرّٰحِمِيْنَ.",
      "transliteration": "Rabbanā āmannā fa-ghfir lanā war-ḥamnā wa Anta khayru-r-rāḥimīn. Ibn Kathir (raḥimahūllāh) explains that forgiveness entails two things: firstly, the sin being concealed by Allah and secondly, not being punished for the sin. And whenever mercy is mentioned along with forgiveness, such as in the du‘ā’ here, it includes the hope that Allah does not permit one to fall into that act again.",
      "translation": "Our Lord, we have believed, so forgive us and have mercy upon us: You are the Best of those who are merciful. (23:109)",
      "virtue": "",
      "reference": "",
      "repetitions": null,
      "order": 7,
      "tags": [
        "Quranic Duas",
        "Forgiveness"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 8,
      "category_id": 11,
      "title": "Duʿa for Forgiveness & Mercy",
      "title_ar": null,
      "arabic": "رَبِّ اغْفِرْ وَارْحَمْ وَأَنْتَ خَيْرُ الرّٰحِمِيْنَ.",
      "transliteration": "Rabbi-ghfir wa-rḥam wa Anta khayru-r-rāḥimīn.",
      "translation": "My Lord, forgive and have mercy. You are the Best of those who are merciful. (23:118)",
      "virtue": "## Hadith\n– Forgive: wipe away my sins and conceal them from people. – Have mercy: Guide me and give me the ability to say and do the correct thing. – The combination of maghfirah (forgiveness) and raḥmah (mercy) is the one most frequently seen in the du‘ās of the Qur‘ān. – This āyah indicates that one should not become deceived with one’s actions, as good deeds can sometimes make one arrogant. Similarly, it is a reminder that one should cling on to the mercy of Allah. (al-Ālūsī) – Raḥmah is mercy, compassion, nurturing love, and kindness.",
      "reference": "",
      "repetitions": null,
      "order": 8,
      "tags": [
        "Quranic Duas",
        "Forgiveness"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 9,
      "category_id": 11,
      "title": "Duʿa of Prophet Nuh ﷺ for Forgiveness",
      "title_ar": null,
      "arabic": "رَبِّ إِنِّيْ أَعُوْذُ بِكَ أَنْ أَسْأَلَكَ مَا لَيْسَ لِيْ بِهِ عِلْمٌ ۖ وَإِلَّا تَغْفِرْ لِيْ وَتَرْحَمْنِيْ أَكُنْ مِّنَ الْخٰسِرِيْنَ.",
      "transliteration": "Rabbi innī aʿūdhu bika an as’alaka mā laysa lī bihī ʿilm, wa il-lā taghfir lī wa tarḥamnī aku-m-mina-l-khāsīrīn. This is the du‘ā’ of Nuḥ (‘alayhis-salām) after Allah admonished him for making du‘ā’ for his son who had drowned in the state of disbelief.",
      "translation": "My Lord, I seek Your protection from asking You anything about which I have no knowledge. And unless You forgive me and have mercy upon me, I shall be amongst the losers. (11:47)",
      "virtue": "## Hadith\n- We see his humility and how he sought Allah’s protection, forgiveness and care. • We learn the importance of learning how to make du‘ā’ correctly so we don’t ask for something we shouldn’t be asking for. • Once again, we see ‘forgiveness + mercy’. They are both critical in the life of every believer and each time we make du‘ā’, we should ask Allah for both of these as they encompass all good. Without them, we will certainly be ‘amongst the losers’.",
      "reference": "",
      "repetitions": null,
      "order": 9,
      "tags": [
        "Quranic Duas",
        "Forgiveness",
        "Prophet"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 10,
      "category_id": 11,
      "title": "Duʿa for Yourself, the Deceased & the Ummah",
      "title_ar": null,
      "arabic": "رَبَّنَا اغْفِرْ لَنَا وَلِإِخْوَانِنَا الَّذِيْنَ سَبَقُوْنَا بِالْإِيْمَانِ ، وَلَا تَجْعَلْ فِيْ قُلُوْبِنَا غِلًّا لِّلَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا رَبَّنَآ إِنَّكَ رَءُوْفٌ رَّحِيْمٌ.",
      "transliteration": "Rabbana-ghfir lanā wa li-ikhwānina-l-ladhīna sabaqūnā bil-īmān, wa lā tajʿal fī qulūbinā ghilla-l-lil-ladhīna āmanū Rabbanā innaka Ra’ūfu-r-Raḥīm.",
      "translation": "Our Lord, forgive us and our brothers who preceded us in faith. Do not put in our hearts any hatred toward those who have believed. Our Lord, indeed You are the Most Compassionate, the Ever-Merciful. (59:10)",
      "virtue": "## Who to Pray For\n\n- **Pray for your brothers and sisters** in faith wherever they may be in the world\n- **Pray for the deceased**: Those who have recently left the world and those who left the world a long time ago, those you personally knew and those whose names may be unknown to you, yet you are tied to them through the bond of imān\n- **Pray for yourself**\n\n## What to Pray For\n\n- **Pray for forgiveness**\n- **Pray for love**\n- **Pray for pure hearts**\n- **Pray for an end** to the hatred, bitterness and infighting amongst the Ummah\n- **Pray for all of the above** through this brief, yet comprehensive duʿā in the Qurʿān",
      "reference": "",
      "repetitions": null,
      "order": 10,
      "tags": [
        "Quranic Duas"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 11,
      "category_id": 11,
      "title": "Duʿa of the Believers on the Day of Judgement",
      "title_ar": null,
      "arabic": "رَبَّنَآ أَتْمِمْ لَنَا نُوْرَنَا وَاغْفِرْ لَنَا ۖ إِنَّكَ عَلَىٰ كُلِّ ��َيْءٍ قَدِيْرٌ.",
      "transliteration": "Rabbanā atmim lanā nūranā wa-ghfir lanā innaka ʿalā kulli shay’in Qadīr.",
      "translation": "Our Lord, perfect for us our light and forgive us. Indeed, You are All-Powerful over everything. (66:08)",
      "virtue": "## The Light of the Day of Judgement\n\nThis is the duʿā the believers will make on the Day of Judgement when the light of the hypocrites will be extinguished. To reach to their ultimate destination, Jannah, this **light (nūr)** will be essential in guiding them to it. This nūr is also the same light which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ will recognize us with.\n\n## Attaining Light in This World\n\nIn order to be rewarded with this nūr in the hereafter, we must strive to attain the **nūr of knowledge, guidance and imān** in this world.\n\n## The Prophet's Dua for Light\n\nThis is why the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would recite the following duʿā on the way to the Masjid:\n\n**اَللّهُمَّ اجْعَلْ فِيْ قَلْبِيْ نُوْرًا ، وَفِيْ بَصَرِيْ نُوْرًا ، وَفِيْ سَمْعِيْ نُوْرًا ، وَعَنْ يَّمِيْنِيْ نُوْرًا ، وَعَنْ يَّسَارِيْ نُوْرًا ، وَفَوْقِيْ نُوْرًا ، وَتَحْتِيْ نُوْرًا ، وَأَمَامِيْ نُوْرًا ، وَخَلْفِيْ نُوْرًا ، وَاجْعَلْ لِيْ نُوْرًا**\n\n\"O Allah, place light in my heart, light in my sight and light in my hearing. Place light on my right and place light on my left. Place light above me and place light beneath me. Place light in front of me, place light behind me and grant me light.\" (Bukhārī)",
      "reference": "",
      "repetitions": null,
      "order": 11,
      "tags": [
        "Quranic Duas"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 12,
      "category_id": 11,
      "title": "Duʿa of Asiya for a House Near Allah in Paradise",
      "title_ar": null,
      "arabic": "رَبِّ ابْنِ لِيْ عِنْدَكَ بَيْتًا فِيْ الْجَنَّةِ.",
      "transliteration": "Rabbi-b-ni lī ʿindaka baytan fi-l-Jannah.",
      "translation": "My Lord, build for me, near You, a house in Paradise. (66:11)",
      "virtue": "## The Story of Asiya\n\nThis is the duʿā of Āsiyā (raḍiy Allāhu ʿanhā), the wife of Pharaoh. This duʿā is a testament to her **imān and yaqīn** in Allah.\n\n## Her Sacrifice\n\nBeing the wife of the most powerful King on the earth, she could have enjoyed the best of what a woman could desire in the world. However:\n- She **gave this up**\n- **Rejected** the glitz and glamour of this world\n- **Chose Allah** over all of this\n- **Resisted** the pressures of her society, the palace, the throne and her own husband\n- **Chose instead** to submit to Allah\n\n## The Reward\n\nAs a result, she suffered greatly for it. But it was **worth it**. It made her **one of the most revered women** across history, and more importantly in the sight of Allah.\n\n## Choosing the Neighbor Before the House\n\nThe scholars mention that by mentioning **'near You' before 'a house'**, she chose her neighbor before the house - what was more important to her was that she enjoys the **proximity and closeness to Allah** than the house itself. This brief, yet powerful duʿā speaks volumes of her deep awareness, love and longing for Him.",
      "reference": "",
      "repetitions": null,
      "order": 12,
      "tags": [
        "Quranic Duas"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 13,
      "category_id": 11,
      "title": "Duʿa for Protection From the Hell-fire",
      "title_ar": null,
      "arabic": "رَبَّنَا اصْرِفْ عَنَّا عَذَابَ جَهَنَّمَ ۖ إِنَّ عَذَابَهَا كَانَ غَرَامًا ، إِنَّهَا سَآءَتْ مُسْتَقَرًّا وَّمُقَامًا.",
      "transliteration": "Rabbana-ṣrif ʿan-nā ʿadhāba Jahannam, inna ʿadhābahā kāna gharāmā. Innahā sā’at mustaqarra-w-wa muqāmā. This du‘ā’ is found at the end of Sūrah al-Furqān, whereby Allah outlines the qualities of the ‘Ibād al-Raḥmān’, the slaves of the Extremely Merciful. One of their qualities is that they invoke Allah with this du‘ā’. This du‘ā’ teaches the importance of fear. Despite being humble in the day and spending the night in qiyām, the true slaves of Allah beg Him to save them from the eternal punishment of the Hell-fire. It reminds one not to be deceived with one’s good deeds and to not become arrogant. al-Ḥasan (raḥimahullāh) said, “They humbled themselves in the day (to the creation), and tired themselves at night (for the Creator), out of their fear of the punishment of the Hell-fire.”",
      "translation": "Our Lord, turn away from us the punishment of Hell-fire. Indeed, its punishment is endless. Indeed it is an evil residence and abode. (25:65-6)",
      "virtue": "",
      "reference": "",
      "repetitions": null,
      "order": 13,
      "tags": [
        "Quranic Duas",
        "Protection"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 14,
      "category_id": 11,
      "title": "Duʿa of Those Who Reflect",
      "title_ar": null,
      "arabic": "رَبَّنَا مَا خَلَقْتَ هَـٰذَا بٰطِلًا ، سُبْحٰنَكَ فَقِنَا عَذَابَ النَّارِ. رَبَّنَآ إِنَّكَ مَنْ تُدْخِلِ النَّارَ فَقَدْ أَخْزَيْتَهُۥ ۖ ، وَمَا لِلظّـٰلِمِيْنَ مِنْ أَنصَارٍ. رَبَّنَآ إِنَّنَا سَمِعْنَا مُنَادِيًا يُّنَادِىْ لِلْإِيْمَـٰنِ أَنْ اٰمِنُوْا بِرَبِّكُمْ فَاٰمَنَّا ۚ ، رَبَّنَا فَاغْفِرْ لَنَا ذُنُوْبَنَا وَكَفِّرْ عَنَّا سَيِّـاٰتِنَا وَتَوَفَّنَا مَعَ الْأَبْرَارِ. رَبَّنَا وَاٰتِنَا مَا وَعَدْتَّنَا عَلَىٰ رُسُلِكَ وَلَا تُخْزِنَا يَوْمَ الْقِيـٰمَةِ ۗ ، إِنَّكَ لَا تُخْلِفُ الْمِيْعَادَ.",
      "transliteration": "Rabbanā mā khalaqta hādhā bāṭilā, subḥānaka faqinā ʿadhāba-n-nār. Rabbanā innaka man tudhkili-n-nāra fa-qad akhzaytah, wa mā li-ẓ-ẓālimīna min anṣār. Rabbanā in-nanā samiʿnā munādiya-y-yunādī lil-īmāni an āminū bi-Rabbikum fa-āmannā, Rabbanā fa-ghfir lanā dhunūbanā wa kaffir ʿannā sayyi’ātinā wa tawaffanā ma-ʿal-abrār. Rabbanā wa ātinā mā wa-ʿadtanā ʿalā rusulika wa lā tukhzinā yawmal-qiyāmah, in-naka lā tukhliful-mīʿād. This is the du‘ā’ of ‘those of understanding’.",
      "translation": "Our Lord, You have not created all this (the heavens and the earth) without purpose- You are free from any defects- so protect us from the torment of the Fire. Our Lord, indeed whoever You admit to the Fire, You have disgraced him, and for the wrongdoers there are no helpers. Our Lord, indeed we have heard a caller calling to faith, \\[saying\\], ‹Believe in your Lord,› so we have believed. Our Lord, forgive us our sins, wipe out our bad deeds, and let us die with the truly righteous. Our Lord, bestow upon us all that You have promised us through Your messengers and do not humiliate us on the Day of Resurrection. Indeed, You never break Your promise. (3:191-4)",
      "virtue": "## Lessons From This Dua\n\n**The importance of reflection** - We should constantly look at the stars, sun, moon, mountains, seas, greenery etc with a fresh pair of eyes and reflect on their Maker\n\n**The intertwined nature of reflection and dhikr** - Dhikr should be accompanied by reflection, and at the same time reflection should make us cry out \"You did not create this in vain Yā Allah!\"\n\n**Understanding purpose** - Reflection (tafakkur) will make us realise that we and the world around us were created for a purpose. We will be held accountable for what we do and if we reject Him, we will be doomed to the Hell-fire. Hence why we make the second part of the duʿā\n\n**Humbling ourselves** - Reflection in Allah's creation around us should make us humble ourselves, submit to Him in fear and beg Him for protection from the Fire\n\n**A powerful comprehensive dua** - A powerful duʿa for forgiveness, good endings and protection on the Day of Judgement",
      "reference": "",
      "repetitions": null,
      "order": 14,
      "tags": [
        "Quranic Duas"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 15,
      "category_id": 11,
      "title": "Duʿa of the Angels for the Believers",
      "title_ar": null,
      "arabic": "رَبَّنَا وَسِعْتَ كُلَّ شَيْءٍ رَّحْمَةً وَّعِلْمًا ، فَاغْفِرْ لِلَّذِيْنَ تَابُوْا وَاتَّبَعُوْا سَبِيْلَكَ وَقِهِمْ عَذَابَ الْجَحِيْمِ. رَبَّنَا وَأَدْخِلْهُمْ جَنَّاتِ عَدْنٍ الَّتِيْ وَعَدْتَّهُمْ وَمَنْ صَلَحَ مِنْ اٰبَآئِهِمْ وَأَزْوَاجِهِمْ وَذُرِّيَّاتِهِمْ ، إِنَّكَ أَنْتَ الْعَزِيْزُ الْحَكِيْمُ. وَقِهِمُ السَّيِّئَاتِ ، وَمَنْ تَقِ السَّيِّئَاتِ يَوْمَئِذٍ فَقَدْ رَحِمْتَهُ ، وَذَٰلِكَ هُوَ الْفَوْزُ الْعَظِيْمُ.",
      "transliteration": "Rabbanā wasiʿta kulla shay’i-r-raḥmata-w-wa ʿilmā, fa-ghfir lil-ladhīna tābū wa-t-tabaʿū sabīlaka wa qihim ʿadhābal-jaḥīm. Rabbanā wa adkhil-hum jannāti ʿadnini-l-latī wa-ʿadtahum wa man ṣalaḥa min ābā’ihim wa azwājihim wa dhurriy-yātihim, innaka Antal-ʿAzīzu-l-Ḥakīm. Wa qihimu-s-sayyi’āt, wa man taqi-s-sayyi’āti yawma’idhin fa-qad raḥimtah, wa dhālika huwal-fawzul-ʿAẓīm.",
      "translation": "Our Lord, You have encompassed all things in mercy and knowledge, so forgive those who have repented and followed Your path, and protect them from the punishment of Hell-fire. Our Lord, admit them to the eternal gardens of Paradise which You have promised them, along with whoever was righteous from their fathers, their spouses and their children. Indeed, You, and only You, are the All-Mighty and All-Wise. Protect them from all evil deeds. You will have bestowed Your mercy on those You protect from the evil deeds on that Day: that is the greatest achievement indeed. (40:7-9)",
      "virtue": "",
      "reference": "",
      "repetitions": null,
      "order": 15,
      "tags": [
        "Quranic Duas"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 16,
      "category_id": 11,
      "title": "Duʿa of Prophet Musa ﷺ Expressing His Dire Need",
      "title_ar": null,
      "arabic": "رَبِّ إِنِّيْ لِمَآ أَنْزَلْتَ إِلَيَّ مِنْ خَيْرٍ فَقِيْرٌ.",
      "transliteration": "Rabbi innī limā anzalta illayya min khayrin faqīr.",
      "translation": "My Lord, truly I am in dire need of any good which You may send me. (28:24)",
      "virtue": "",
      "reference": "",
      "repetitions": null,
      "order": 16,
      "tags": [
        "Quranic Duas",
        "Prophet"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 17,
      "category_id": 11,
      "title": "The Most Frequent Duʿa of the Prophet ﷺ",
      "title_ar": null,
      "arabic": "رَبَّنَآ اٰتِنَا فِي الدُّنْيَا حَسَنَةً وَّفِي الْآخِرَةِ حَسَنَةً وَّقِنَا عَذَابَ النَّارِ.",
      "transliteration": "Rabbanā ātinā fi-d-dunyā ḥasanah wa fil-ākhirati ḥasanah wa qinā ʿadhāba-n-Nār.",
      "translation": "Our Lord, grant us good in this world and good in the Hereafter, and protect us from the torment of the Fire. (2:201)",
      "virtue": "## Hadith\nAnas (raḍiy Allāhu ‘anhu) narrates that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would supplicate with [the above]. (Bukhārī 4522) In another narration, Qatāda (raḥimahullāh) asked Anas (raḍiy Allāhu ‘anhu) which supplication the Messenger of Allah ﷺ frequently made. He said: “The supplication that the Prophet ﷺ made very frequently is [the above]. He (Qatāda) said that whenever Anas had to supplicate he made this very supplication, and whenever he (intended) to make another supplication he (added) this supplication in it too.” (Muslim 2690) Some of the companions of Anas (raḍiy Allāhu ‘anhu) requested him to supplicate for them. So he supplicated with the [the above] blessed supplication. He then said: “If Allah grants you that (good in this world and good in the Hereafter), then He has granted you ‘all’ goodness.” (Fatḥ al-Bārī)",
      "reference": "Bukhārī 4522",
      "repetitions": null,
      "order": 17,
      "tags": [
        "Quranic Duas",
        "Prophet"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 18,
      "category_id": 11,
      "title": "Duʿa of the People of the Cave for Mercy & Guidance",
      "title_ar": null,
      "arabic": "رَبَّنَآ اٰتِنَا مِنْ لَّدُنْكَ رَحْمَةً وَّهَيِّئْ لَنَا مِنْ أَمْرِنَا رَشَدًا.",
      "transliteration": "Rabbanā ātinā mi-l-ladunka raḥmatan wa hayyi’ lanā min amrinā rashadā.",
      "translation": "Our Lord, grant us from Yourself mercy and provide us with guidance in our matter. (18:10)",
      "virtue": "",
      "reference": "",
      "repetitions": null,
      "order": 18,
      "tags": [
        "Quranic Duas"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 19,
      "category_id": 11,
      "title": "Duʿa for the Firmness of the Heart",
      "title_ar": null,
      "arabic": "رَبَّنَا لَا تُزِغْ قُلُوْبَنَا بَعْدَ إِذْ هَدَيْتَنَا وَهَبْ لَنَا مِنْ لَّدُنْكَ رَحْمَةً ۚ إِنَّكَ أَنتَ الْوَهَّابُ.",
      "transliteration": "Rabbanā lā tuzigh qulūbanā baʿda idh hadayatanā, wa hab lanā mi-l-ladunka raḥmah, innaka Anta-l-Wahhāb.",
      "translation": "Our Lord, do not let our hearts swerve from the truth after You have guided us, and bestow upon us mercy from Yourself. Surely, You, and You Alone are the Great Bestower. (3:8)",
      "virtue": "",
      "reference": "",
      "repetitions": null,
      "order": 19,
      "tags": [
        "Quranic Duas"
      ]
    },
